    <unit id="=&gt;q13" name="=&gt;q13">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">26</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::[Biology] The body's pale and cold, and pretty stiff, meaning rigor mortis has set in. You take a look at some of the exposed back and notice moderate suggillation - that is, the pooling of blood inside the body. The amount of pooled blood and its location, combined with what you deduced so far, tells you that death occured no more than six hours ago.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;q14" name="=&gt;q14">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">28</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::[Chemistry] Additionally, the body reeks of rotten hopper eggs and ammonia - essentially sewage. Looking at the muck on the deceased's clothes confirms that this person has indeed ventured into some rather foul place or places.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
